                                Gloucestershire, Guild of Kalendars in the church of All
                                Saints</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval
                                Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the
                                Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                                Britain index card records the following information, which was
                                deemed unsatisfactory for an attribution: <q>Liber milonis abbatis
                                    Egonyshamie et landavensis episcopi [d. 1516]</q> (at
                                beginning).The ascription to the Gild in <title>Transactions of the
                                    Bristol and Glocestershire Archaeological Society</title> XXXI
                                (1908) 88-9 seems very dubious.</p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">In 1964, Ker reported the location of
                            this book as Bristol, All Saints' Church. It is now in the Bristol
                            Archives.</provenance>
